sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: complete captured Caddy publication, official cfgmgmt file and pinned SSH argv. docs/reference/caddy-configuration.md#native-publication.
  %% Tightened: flow-tighten rules 9, 14, 22. No result printer. The official file check feeds the native end assertion.
  %% status: reviewed
  %% command: none · Node Caddy build
  %% kind: route.caddy_converge
  autonumber
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>workflow execution
  participant N as Target Node<br/>over SSH
  Note over GW: Render, record intent<br/>whole-Node Caddyfile
  %%> When:
  %%> - an operator runs `orbit:caddy-build NODE` on the Gateway; there is no CLI command
  %%> Refused before a task starts:
  %%> - the Node is unknown, the render has a problem (`caddy.render_failed`), or the Node has no SSH address, user or host key, or the control identity is missing (`swamp.ssh_target_unavailable`, `swamp.ssh_identity_unavailable`)
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-route-caddy
  %%> What the operator gets:
  %%> - the Operation ID at once; completion is read from the Operation
  Note over SW: Read the input
  %%> Why first:
  %%> - the captured content hash is verified before the Node is contacted
  SW->>N: Check the connection
  SW->>N: Write the Caddyfile
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - writes the rendered bytes to a run-scoped candidate beside `/etc/caddy/Caddyfile`, `root:caddy`, mode 0640
  SW->>N: Validate the Caddyfile
  %%> Why:
  %%> - `caddy validate` runs as the `caddy` user against the candidate, then atomic rename publishes it; failure leaves the live file unchanged and skips reload
  SW->>N: Reload Caddy
  SW->>N: Check the Caddyfile
  Note over SW: Check the publication
  alt every step succeeds
    SW-->>GW: Native terminal status<br/>captured publication
    Note over GW: Record the version<br/>after the end check
  else a step fails
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>error_code, failed step
    Note over GW: Record the failure
    %%> On the Node:
    %%> - validation failure removes the candidate and keeps the live file; after publication, reload or end-check failure leaves the validated new file
    %%> Retry:
    %%> - fix the cause and run `orbit:caddy-build NODE` again; a Caddyfile that fails validation needs the stored intent corrected first
  end
